meta {
  name: 01 Quote seats
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/centers/me/subscription/quote
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "seats": 10
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.unitPriceXaf: eq 4800
  res.body.amountXaf: eq 48000
}

docs {
  What 10 seats would cost. Run `Center Auth / 03 Login` first.

  Standard pricing is 4,800 XAF a seat with a minimum of 10, so the smallest
  order is 48,000 XAF. A partner center pays 4,500 and quotes 45,000 for the
  same 10 seats — the difference comes from that center's own billing terms,
  not from anything in this request.

  ## The checks that matter

  THE PRICE IS NOT AN INPUT. Every one of these must return 400
  VALIDATION_ERROR, not a quote:

  - `{"seats": 10, "unitPriceXaf": 1}`
  - `{"seats": 10, "amountXaf": 1}`
  - `{"seats": 10, "amount": 1}`
  - `{"seats": 10, "total": 1}`
  - `{"seats": 10, "currency": "EUR"}`
  - `{"seats": 10, "centerId": "some-other-center"}`

  They are REFUSED, not ignored. Quietly dropping an `amount` would leave a
  client believing it had set the price.

  ## The two floors

  - `{"seats": 9}` -> 400 SEATS_BELOW_MINIMUM, with `requiredSeats: 10`
  - with 12 students provisioned, `{"seats": 10}` -> 400
    SEATS_BELOW_STUDENT_COUNT, with `requiredSeats: 12`

  Two different problems needing two different actions, so they carry
  different codes. `requiredSeats` is the number to send next; without it a
  center can only guess.

  To see the second one, provision students past 10 first via
  `Center Students / 02 Provision student`.

  ## Also worth trying

  - `{"seats": "10"}` -> 400. A JSON body has real numbers; a string seat
    count is a client bug worth reporting rather than silently repairing.
  - `{"seats": 20000}` -> 400 SEATS_ABOVE_MAXIMUM. The cap exists because
    amount_xaf is a 32-bit integer, and around 447,000 seats the total would
    overflow the column rather than fail cleanly.

  ## While BLOCKED

  This still works. Finding out what you owe is the first step of paying, and
  a blocked center that cannot take it never comes back. Block the center per
  `Subscription Access / 00 How to block and restore` and re-run — you still
  get a quote.
}
